    "title": "Feds Turn Up at Northwest Miami Used-Car Lot, Snap Pics, Cuff Men Before Dawn - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Livi Miller ,\n5 hours ago Northwest Miami woke up to a federal show of force early Wednesday, as FBI agents converged on a used-car dealership and auto-repair shop, circling vehicles, peering inside and briefly putting two men in handcuffs before letting them go. The focus was Cube Motors on Northwest 79th Street between Third and Fourth avenues, according to people at the scene. No roadways were reported closed, and the FBI would say only that it was carrying out “court-ordered law enforcement activity” in the area. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 2",
